# {{name}}-api

Beginner-friendly, production-style Go API service scaffold for Turborepo.

## What is included

- `cmd/{{name}}-api`: clean entrypoint with graceful shutdown
- `internal/config`: env-driven config
- `internal/observability`: structured logger
- `internal/httpapi`: router, middleware, API implementation
- `api/openapi.yaml`: single source of truth for API contract
- Go server types/interfaces generated with `oapi-codegen`
- Frontend SDK generated into `packages/{{name}}-sdk`

## First run

```bash
pnpm --filter @umpa/{{name}}-api gen
pnpm --filter @umpa/{{name}}-api dev
```

## Quality loop

```bash
pnpm --filter @umpa/{{name}}-api format
pnpm --filter @umpa/{{name}}-api lint
pnpm --filter @umpa/{{name}}-api test
pnpm --filter @umpa/{{name}}-api build
```

## Turbo usage

```bash
pnpm turbo run test --filter=@umpa/{{name}}-api
pnpm turbo run build --filter=@umpa/{{name}}-api
```

## API contract workflow

1. Update `api/openapi.yaml`.
2. Run `pnpm --filter @umpa/{{name}}-api gen`.
3. Backend interfaces/models and frontend SDK are regenerated from one source.

## Environment

Copy `.env.example` into `.env` and adjust values.
